    "preferred": "The interesting leaves usually have seven lobes, occasionally five or nine lobes, varying widely in size from 7 to 12 cm long and from 6 to 11 cm wide. The lobes are widely separated more than three-quarters of the way to the leaf base. They spread slightly and are sometimes twisted at various angles. The lobes are narrow, almost Corvallis to a sturdy, medium-sized tree up to 5 m tall. A different transliteration system from Japanese to English gives this cultivar the slightly different name of"
